      "description": "Career Preparation - Beacon College Search About Why Beacon Why Beacon? Beacon by the Numbers The Life Abundant Leadership President Hagerty Leadership Presidential Search Campus & Community Our Campus Our Community Mason Art Gallery Directory Accreditation Strategic Plan Policies Student Handbook Title VI Title IX Reasonable Modification Policy Disabilities Accommodations Policy Family Guide Privacy Policy Clery Report About Founded in 1989, Beacon College in Leesburg, Florida, stands as a shining beacon of hope and opportunity for students with learning disabilities. Admissions & Aid Learn More & Apply Apply New Students Transfer Students International Students Homeschooled Students Parents and Families Educators Admitted Students Affordability Tuition & Fees Scholarships Financial Aid Financial Aid FAQs Other Financial Resources CARES Act Get to Know Us Admissions Events Plan a Visit Meet the Admissions Staff Download Brochures Request Information New Student Orientation Admissions & Aid Join us on campus for one of our upcoming Open House event on Sept. 26! We invite you to experience the personalized support, vibrant campus life, and academic excellence that make Beacon College the ideal choice for students with learning differences. Register Now > College Readiness Programs & Options Summer for Success College Edge Navigator PREP Intro to College Academics College Coaching Beacon Foundations Dual Enrollment Resources & Tools Choosing the Right Program Meet the Experts Free Downloadable Tools Webinar Recordings Partnerships Partner With Us Certificate in Coaching Adolescents Neurodiversity in Higher Ed Certificate College Readiness Beacon College’s Center for College Readiness draws on our successful 35-year history of working exclusively with students who learn differently through seven unique programs for students and families through hands-on learning and one-to-one coaching. Academics Academic Programs Anthrozoology Business Management Hospitality and Tourism Computer Information Systems Design and Digital Media Early Childhood and Elementary Education Humanities Human Services Psychology Studio Arts Minors Success & Support Services Academic Advising Academic Support Career Preparation Career Treks Internships Study Abroad Resources Course Catalog Academic Calendars Registrar’s Office Academics Intellectual challenge is at the heart of a Beacon education. We take this very seriously, but we are also very practical about it. Our 10 bachelor’s degree programs are intended to prepare our students to find worthy work in today’s global marketplace.  Additionally, we encourage students to explore their diverse interests through one or more of our 17 minors. Student Life Campus Life Life at Beacon First Year Experience Housing Dining Services Transportation Health and Wellness Safety Activities Activities and Clubs Fitness and Recreation Athletics Athletics Men’s Basketball Women’s Basketball Cross Country and Track Golf Student Life “Pursuing the life abundant” is the pervading theme that infuses everything we do at Beacon College. It’s something we take very seriously indeed. At Beacon, you’ll be able to be the most that you can be. Both within the classroom and far beyond it, we nurture a vivacious learning laboratory that calls upon you to seek and cherish all of life’s richness. News & Events News & Media News and Updates Lighting the Path Newsletter A World of Difference Office of Communications Events Salon Series Family Weekend Alumni Weekend Commencement News & Events We are committed to keeping you up to date. Check out current news, media, and upcoming events from Beacon College. Quick Links Parents Students Educators Alumni Visit Campus Request Information Apply Give Portals Canvas Email MyBeacon Parent Portal Online Bill Pay Faculty/Staff E-Flame The HUB Faculty/Staff MyBeacon Directory Library Resources for: Parents Students Educators Alumni Visit Campus Request Information Apply Give Portals Canvas Email MyBeacon Parent Portal Online Bill Pay Faculty/Staff E-Flame The HUB Faculty/Staff MyBeacon Directory Library About Why Beacon Why Beacon? Beacon by the Numbers The Life Abundant Leadership President Hagerty Leadership Presidential Search Campus & Community Our Campus Our Community Mason Art Gallery Directory Accreditation Strategic Plan Policies Student Handbook Title VI Title IX Reasonable Modification Policy Disabilities Accommodations Policy Family Guide Privacy Policy Clery Report About Founded in 1989, Beacon College in Leesburg, Florida, stands as a shining beacon of hope and opportunity for students with learning disabilities. Admissions & Aid Learn More & Apply Apply New Students Transfer Students International Students Homeschooled Students Parents and Families Educators Admitted Students Affordability Tuition & Fees Scholarships Financial Aid Financial Aid FAQs Other Financial Resources CARES Act Get to Know Us Admissions Events Plan a Visit Meet the Admissions Staff Download Brochures Request Information New Student Orientation Admissions & Aid Join us on campus for one of our upcoming Open House event on Sept. 26! We invite you to experience the personalized support, vibrant campus life, and academic excellence that make Beacon College the ideal choice for students with learning differences. Register Now > College Readiness Programs & Options Summer for Success College Edge Navigator PREP Intro to College Academics College Coaching Beacon Foundations Dual Enrollment Resources & Tools Choosing the Right Program Meet the Experts Free Downloadable Tools Webinar Recordings Partnerships Partner With Us Certificate in Coaching Adolescents Neurodiversity in Higher Ed Certificate College Readiness Beacon College’s Center for College Readiness draws on our successful 35-year history of working exclusively with students who learn differently through seven unique programs for students and families through hands-on learning and one-to-one coaching. Academics Academic Programs Anthrozoology Business Management Hospitality and Tourism Computer Information Systems Design and Digital Media Early Childhood and Elementary Education Humanities Human Services Psychology Studio Arts Minors Success & Support Services Academic Advising Academic Support Career Preparation Career Treks Internships Study Abroad Resources Course Catalog Academic Calendars Registrar’s Office Academics Intellectual challenge is at the heart of a Beacon education. We take this very seriously, but we are also very practical about it. Our 10 bachelor’s degree programs are intended to prepare our students to find worthy work in today’s global marketplace.  Additionally, we encourage students to explore their diverse interests through one or more of our 17 minors. Student Life Campus Life Life at Beacon First Year Experience Housing Dining Services Transportation Health and Wellness Safety Activities Activities and Clubs Fitness and Recreation Athletics Athletics Men’s Basketball Women’s Basketball Cross Country and Track Golf Student Life “Pursuing the life abundant” is the pervading theme that infuses everything we do at Beacon College. It’s something we take very seriously indeed. At Beacon, you’ll be able to be the most that you can be. Both within the classroom and far beyond it, we nurture a vivacious learning laboratory that calls upon you to seek and cherish all of life’s richness. News & Events News & Media News and Updates Lighting the Path Newsletter A World of Difference Office of Communications Events Salon Series Family Weekend Alumni Weekend Commencement News & Events We are committed to keeping you up to date. Check out current news, media, and upcoming events from Beacon College. Search Career Preparation Home Academics Career Preparation Juan and Lisa Jones Center for Career Preparation Your education at Beacon sets the stage for your career adventure, and we’re here to help our students and alumni navigate this great journey! Beacon’s unique career advising program starts the day you begin at the college. With the career team at the Juan and Lisa Jones Center for Career Preparation, you’ll have a dedicated career advisor assigned to you who will help you develop professional assets and access the latest tools and personalized career resources, such as Handshake and Big Interview. Your career team will also engage you in a variety of interactive career events both in-person (on and off campus) and through virtual opportunities with local, regional, and national partners. Internship Requirements On Campus Student Employment Career Treks Handshake Big Interview Beacon Career Closet 2.0 Career Center Newsletters Fiona Clifford, a junior majoring in Human Services with an education minor, earned her Registered Behavior Technician (RBT) Certificate for her ABA Behavioral Technician role! She completed the 40-hour course which is a nationally recognized paraprofessional certification in behavior analysis. Pierre Bernard works with a giraffe during his summer internship with the Caldwell Zoo in Texas where he participated in 1:1 animal care on the Mammal Team by preparing the daily diet and clearing brush to feed elephants more naturally while observing other species and interacting with zoo guests. Quinn Bullock Beverly interned with The AES Corp, through Broad Futures (a nonprofit organization based in Washington, D.C. that provides internship opportunities for neurodivergent students). At AES, he contributed to the improvement of the AES guest WiFi access portal from a User Experience perspective by collaborating with key users and technical team members. He also created a Knowledge Article soon to be attached to the web portal to provide instructions for the end users. Ben Sweetland participates in a 1:1 virtual interview with a Southwest Airlines recruiter to learn more about their neurodiverse internships for their Information Technology department. Skill Up Today Fiona Clifford, a junior majoring in Human Services with an education minor, earned her Registered Behavior Technician (RBT) Certificate for her ABA Behavioral Technician role! She completed the 40-hour course which is a nationally recognized paraprofessional certification in behavior analysis. Wild Adventures Pierre Bernard works with a giraffe during his summer internship with the Caldwell Zoo in Texas where he participated in 1:1 animal care on the Mammal Team by preparing the daily diet and clearing brush to feed elephants more naturally while observing other species and interacting with zoo guests. Unlocking Future Paths Quinn Bullock Beverly interned with The AES Corp, through Broad Futures (a nonprofit organization based in Washington, D.C. that provides internship opportunities for neurodivergent students). At AES, he contributed to the improvement of the AES guest WiFi access portal from a User Experience perspective by collaborating with key users and technical team members. He also created a Knowledge Article soon to be attached to the web portal to provide instructions for the end users. Breaking Barriers Ben Sweetland participates in a 1:1 virtual interview with a Southwest Airlines recruiter to learn more about their neurodiverse internships for their Information Technology department. Career Treks 2026 Summer Experiential Learning Program in Leesburg You can participate in Beacon’s intensive career-focused summer program – Career Treks! You’ll be exposed to different career opportunities and embark on field trips to some of Florida’s largest companies and nonprofits. Career Treks provides skills-based learning options and delves into more than simply job titles helping you find your career path. Career Treks Shake Hands and Interview Big You’ll be connected to the latest career resources through our career center team. At your fingertips, you’ll be able to connect with thousands of internships and job opportunities through Handshake , our all-in-one career management system. Additionally, you’ll have access to Big Interview , our new interview practice system that leverages AI and human feedback. All of these resources are FREE for students! Handshake Through Handshake, you’ll schedule appointments with your career advisor, set up individualized job searches, store resumes and e-portfolios, and register for career events. Handshake is designed exclusively for college students — and used by every Beacon student! Register Today Big Interview With Big Interview, you’ll be able to participate in our new interview practice system that leverages video with Artificial Intelligence (AI) and human feedback. From internships to early careers and graduate school to scholarships, Big Interview helps to better prepare you for every type of professional interview. Our career center team is ready to assist you with this unique resource that mirrors hiring practices now being used across industries nationwide. Register Today Confidence Styled Give them another reason to hire you! Beacon’s Career Closet 2.0 makes career apparel stylish, simple, and accessible for students and alumni. The Juan and Lisa Jones Center for Career Preparation has partnered with Hyde to bring you a professional styling and subscription service delivered to your door. Students and alumni can speak with one of Hyde’s expert stylists, receive professional guidance on what to wear for interviews and events, and then get an entire outfit delivered straight to their door. With access to affordable professional and casual attire that they can keep for 30 days, with no pressure to buy anything, students can rent suitable clothing options for interviews or internships. Let Hyde worry about your outfit so you can focus your attention on what really matters, nailing the interview or internship. Additionally, our Getzel wardrobe for men and Admire for ladies is a Professional (GAP) wardrobe resource room for Beacon students that helps you fill in any “gaps” you may have when needing to dress for success for career fairs, interviews, and the workplace. With a wide selection of suits, blazers, skirts/slacks, ties, and button-down shirts, you’ll make that first impression a positive step as you enter the professional world for any of your short-term events. To visit the GAP Closet, please check in at the Career Center using the Handshake kiosk. Learn More! Career Development: More In Four+ At Beacon, your career development path is critical to us, so you’ll participate in a four-year career development program in your journey towards your bachelor’s degree. Through a combination of coursework and engagement, our More in Four+ approach helps you learn more than just career options. Our program concentrates on identifying your values, strengths, and goals; further developing your professional communication skills and work attitudes; preparing resumes; honing interview skills; and understanding the ever-changing industry trends as you seek career opportunities after graduation. From job shadowing to internships and experiential learning to career fairs, you’ll be prepared for a successful transition from college to the workplace or graduate school. Our job is to help prepare you, not just for your first job but to successfully navigate a career journey that is constantly evolving. Do you have career questions? Confident in your career vision? Still unsure of what you want to do after college? Just like you, every question matters — no matter what your stage in life or your age when you ask the question. Let us help you develop your blueprint for your career plans and envision the kind of life you want through hard work and persistence. Career Preparation News Beacon News Virtual ZooTampa Internship May 18, 2026 Charlie Ige, a rising senior, is observing animal behavior at ZooTampa at Lowry Park as part of her studies for a degree in anthrozoology. Career Development Summer Internships and Big Adventures May 11, 2026 Beacon College students are heading to summer internships that will help prepare them for future careers as they network, build connections, learn new skills and gain hands-on experience. Career Development Cert Saturdays! February 3, 2026 Beacon College is reaching a growing number of students with new opportunities to build professional credentials for the workplace — from math and public speaking to first aid and computer certifications. Employers: Discover Your Future Talent Pipeline with Beacon College Employer engagement takes place across our campus and our community through physical events — like our annual ICAN career fair — and on digital platforms with online training sessions, employer info sessions, and Handshake appointments. Our Beacon career team is here to assist your recruitment efforts to identify talented, neurodiverse candidates for your internship and early career opportunities with your business/organization. We’re here to help you find your next great coworker! Reach out to our career team today for your internship and early career hiring needs at 352-638-9808 or careercenter@beaconcollege.edu . Alumni Career Assistance 13 Average number of jobs held by a worker through their retirement 4 Average number of years spent at a position Your career path will lead to multiple job opportunities, and Beacon is here to support you through a variety of career transitions. Our Career Center’s alumni services include access to Handshake, Big Interview , career counseling, resume review, Beacon’s Career Closet 2.0 and much more. Wherever you call home today, Beacon alumni can be supported by an assigned career advisor through in-person meetings (for local alumni) or virtual meetings. Reach out to our career center team today at 352-638-9808 or careercenter@beaconcollege.edu . Connect With Us Beacon Facebook Visit Us Beacon YouTube Visit Us Beacon Twitter Visit Us Beacon LinkedIn Visit Us Beacon Instagram Visit Us Career Prep LinkedIn Visit Us Career Prep Instagram Visit Us Meet the Juan and Lisa Jones Center for Career Preparation Team Melissa Bradley Executive Director of Center for Career Preparation 352-787-1658 mbradley@beaconcollege.edu Blanca Delucio Student Employment Coordinator 352-638-9732 bdelucio@beaconcollege.edu Marissa Esty Career Advisor 352-805-1296 mesty@beaconcollege.edu Faith Otero Career Advisor 352-638-9826 fotero@beaconcollege.edu Brianna Rivera Program Assistant 352-638-9808 brivera1@beaconcollege.edu Apply Today Request Info Plan a Visit RESOURCES Directory Campus Map Alumni Email Portal MyBeacon Portal Canvas Tech Support For Media WORKING AT BEACON Career Opportunities Faculty/Staff Portal Student Employment Giving Beacon College’s EASE Grant Performance Measures If you’re having accessibility issues, please let us know . Contact Us (855) 220-5374 Address 105 East Main Street Leesburg, Florida 34748 Follow Us © 2026 Beacon College. Web Design by PHOS Creative Sitemap Privacy Policy Accessibility Title VI Title IX"
    },
