 Hospitality and Tourism Computer Information Systems Design and Digital Media Early Childhood and Elementary Education Humanities Human Services Psychology Studio Arts Minors Success & Support Services Academic Advising Academic Support Career Preparation Career Treks Internships Study Abroad Resources Course Catalog Academic Calendars Registrar’s Office Academics Intellectual challenge is at the heart of a Beacon education. We take this very seriously, but we are also very practical about it. Our 10 bachelor’s degree programs are intended to prepare our students to find worthy work in today’s global marketplace.  Additionally, we encourage students to explore their diverse interests through one or more of our 17 minors. Student Life Campus Life Life at Beacon First Year Experience Housing Dining Services Transportation Health and Wellness Safety Activities Activities and Clubs Fitness and Recreation Athletics Athletics Men’s Basketball Women’s Basketball Cross Country and Track Golf Student Life “Pursuing the life abundant” is the pervading theme that infuses everything we do at Beacon College. It’s something we take very seriously indeed. At Beacon, you’ll be able to be the most that you can be. Both within the classroom and far beyond it, we nurture a vivacious learning laboratory that calls upon you to seek and cherish all of life’s richness. News & Events News & Media News and Updates Lighting the Path Newsletter A World of Difference Office of Communications Events Salon Series Family Weekend Alumni Weekend Commencement News & Events We are committed to keeping you up to date. Check out current news, media, and upcoming events from Beacon College. Quick Links Parents Students Educators Alumni Visit Campus Request Information Apply Give Portals Canvas Email MyBeacon Parent Portal Online Bill Pay Faculty/Staff E-Flame The HUB Faculty/Staff MyBeacon Directory Library Resources for: Parents Students Educators Alumni Visit Campus Request Information Apply Give Portals Canvas Email MyBeacon Parent Portal Online Bill Pay Faculty/Staff E-Flame The HUB Faculty/Staff MyBeacon Directory Library About Why Beacon Why Beacon? Beacon by the Numbers The Life Abundant Leadership President Hagerty Leadership Presidential Search Campus & Community Our Campus Our Community Mason Art Gallery Directory Accreditation Strategic Plan Policies Student Handbook Title VI Title IX Reasonable Modification Policy Disabilities Accommodations Policy Family Guide Privacy Policy Clery Report About Founded in 1989, Beacon College in Leesburg, Florida, stands as a shining beacon of hope and opportunity for students with learning disabilities. Admissions & Aid Learn More & Apply Apply New Students Transfer Students International Students Homeschooled Students Parents and Families Educators Admitted Students Affordability Tuition & Fees Scholarships Financial Aid Financial Aid FAQs Other Financial Resources CARES Act Get to Know Us Admissions Events Plan a Visit Meet the Admissions Staff Download Brochures Request Information New Student Orientation Admissions & Aid Join us on campus for one of our upcoming Open House event on Sept. 26! We invite you to experience the personalized support, vibrant campus life, and academic excellence that make Beacon College the ideal choice for students with learning differences. Register Now > College Readiness Programs & Options Summer for Success College Edge Navigator PREP Intro to College Academics College Coaching Beacon Foundations Dual Enrollment Resources & Tools Choosing the Right Program Meet the Experts Free Downloadable Tools Webinar Recordings Partnerships Partner With Us Certificate in Coaching Adolescents Neurodiversity in Higher Ed Certificate College Readiness Beacon College’s Center for College Readiness draws on our successful 35-year history of working exclusively with students who learn differently through seven unique programs for students and families through hands-on learning and one-to-one coaching. Academics Academic Programs Anthrozoology Business Management Hospitality and Tourism Computer Information Systems Design and Digital Media Early Childhood and Elementary Education Humanities Human Services Psychology Studio Arts Minors Success & Support Services Academic Advising Academic Support Career Preparation Career Treks Internships Study Abroad Resources Course Catalog Academic Calendars Registrar’s Office Academics Intellectual challenge is at the heart of a Beacon education. We take this very seriously, but we are also very practical about it. Our 10 bachelor’s degree programs are intended to prepare our students to find worthy work in today’s global marketplace.  Additionally, we encourage students to explore their diverse interests through one or more of our 17 minors. Student Life Campus Life Life at Beacon First Year Experience Housing Dining Services Transportation Health and Wellness Safety Activities Activities and Clubs Fitness and Recreation Athletics Athletics Men’s Basketball Women’s Basketball Cross Country and Track Golf Student Life “Pursuing the life abundant” is the pervading theme that infuses everything we do at Beacon College. It’s something we take very seriously indeed. At Beacon, you’ll be able to be the most that you can be. Both within the classroom and far beyond it, we nurture a vivacious learning laboratory that calls upon you to seek and cherish all of life’s richness. News & Events News & Media News and Updates Lighting the Path Newsletter A World of Difference Office of Communications Events Salon Series Family Weekend Alumni Weekend Commencement News & Events We are committed to keeping you up to date. Check out current news, media, and upcoming events from Beacon College. Search Summer for Success Home College Readiness Programs Summer for Success Your Adventure Begins This Summer July 12 – July 31, 2026 Ready for an unforgettable summer? At Beacon's Summer for Success, you won’t just learn—you’ll level up ! Spend three weeks living on a college campus, exploring new interests, and building the confidence and skills to take on your future. Whether you’re mapping out your college game plan or just looking for a summer that’s fun, challenging, and different, this is your chance to discover how you learn best, tackle new challenges, and make lasting friendships along the way. If you're a high school student who learns differently , this program is designed to help you build independence, understand your strengths, and get the tools you need to succeed in high school and college—all while having an incredible summer. Apply Now Popular tracks and courses will fill up — apply early to secure your spot! Begin Application Information Session Learn more and ask questions at a live info session with the program director. Register Now Chat with Us Meet with us virtually one-on-one to ask questions or see if this program is right for you! Schedule a Chat Choose your own adventure! We have three exciting track options to help you explore what excites you while building the confidence, skills, and independence to take on your future. Discover new passions, tackle creative challenges, and get a taste of different fields in our Exploration Track Immerse yourself in the world of tourism and entertainment in our Entertainment Track Connect with animals and explore wildlife science in our Anthrozoology Track No matter which you choose, you’ll make unforgettable memories, connect with new friends from across the country, and gain real-world skills that set you up for success—all while having the best summer ever. College is for discovering new interests and building confidence in your strengths—and that’s exactly what the Exploration Track is all about! Choose from 24 unique hands-on, interactive courses designed to spark curiosity and challenge you in exciting ways. From psychology to digital media, creative writing to zoology, gaming to business —no matter what subjects you choose, you’ll discover new talents, gain confidence in your learning style, and leave with a better sense of where your future could take you . Explore All Course Options Orlando is the world’s premier destination for unforgettable experiences—but what makes these attractions so successful? The Hospitality Track takes you behind the scenes of the entertainment capital of America, exploring the tourism, hospitality, and creative industries that make Orlando magical. This immersive track combines classroom learning with field experiences at Disney’s four theme parks and other Orlando attractions. You’ll discover the history and business of entertainment, learn about guest experience design, and explore career paths in hospitality, tourism, and event planning. Through behind-the-scenes tours, guest speakers, and hands-on activities , you’ll gain insight into why millions visit Orlando annually and what it takes to create experiences that leave a lasting impact! Discover the fascinating world of human-animal relationships in our Anthrozoology Track . This unique program explores the science, ethics, and practices of working with animals across various settings and contexts. In this track, you’ll engage in hands-on learning experiences with different animal species, learn from expert instructors, and explore potential career paths in animal care, conservation, and research. Whether you’re interested in veterinary science, wildlife management, or simply have a passion for animals, this track offers valuable insights and skills for your future. Through field trips, practical workshops, and collaborative projects , you’ll develop a deeper understanding of animal behavior, welfare, and the important role animals play in our world. 2026 Track Options Choose your own adventure! We have three exciting track options to help you explore what excites you while building the confidence, skills, and independence to take on your future. Discover new passions, tackle creative challenges, and get a taste of different fields in our Exploration Track Immerse yourself in the world of tourism and entertainment in our Entertainment Track Connect with animals and explore wildlife science in our Anthrozoology Track No matter which you choose, you’ll make unforgettable memories, connect with new friends from across the country, and gain real-world skills that set you up for success—all while having the best summer ever. Exploration Track: Try Something New, Find What You Love College is for discovering new interests and building confidence in your strengths—and that’s exactly what the Exploration Track is all about! Choose from 24 unique hands-on, interactive courses designed to spark curiosity and challenge you in exciting ways. From psychology to digital media, creative writing to zoology, gaming to business —no matter what subjects you choose, you’ll discover new talents, gain confidence in your learning style, and leave with a better sense of where your future could take you . Explore All Course Options Entertainment Track: The Magic Behind the Experience Orlando is the world’s premier destination for unforgettable experiences—but what makes these attractions so successful? The Hospitality Track takes you behind the scenes of the entertainment capital of America, exploring the tourism, hospitality, and creative industries that make Orlando magical. This immersive track combines classroom learning with field experiences at Disney’s four theme parks and other Orlando attractions. You’ll discover the history and business of entertainment, learn about guest experience design, and explore career paths in hospitality, tourism, and event planning. Through behind-the-scenes tours, guest speakers, and hands-on activities , you’ll gain insight into why millions visit Orlando annually and what it takes to create experiences that leave a lasting impact! Anthrozoology Track: Exploring the Human-Animal Connection Discover the fascinating world of human-animal relationships in our Anthrozoology Track . This unique program explores the science, ethics, and practices of working with animals across various settings and contexts. In this track, you’ll engage in hands-on learning experiences with different animal species, learn from expert instructors, and explore potential career paths in animal care, conservation, and research. Whether you’re interested in veterinary science, wildlife management, or simply have a passion for animals, this track offers valuable insights and skills for your future. Through field trips, practical workshops, and collaborative projects , you’ll develop a deeper understanding of animal behavior, welfare, and the important role animals play in our world. Introducing Our New Anthrozoology Track for 2026! Do you have a special bond with animals? Our Anthrozoology Track offers a comprehensive exploration of human-animal relationships through three specialized courses. Explore animal husbandry and welfare science or take your passion into the field observing local wildlife. Or grab your zookeeper hat for an adventure through the fascinating realms of animal development, evolution, and classification while exploring zoology. This track combines classroom learning with hands-on experiences to prepare you for fields of study that work with animals. Beyond the Classroom: Social, Fun, and Adventure Your experience doesn’t stop when class ends! Afternoons and evenings are filled with activities that help you unwind, connect with new friends, and have fun, including: ✨ Fitness center workouts, gaming lounges, movie nights, and talent showcases 🎢 Weekend trips to top Orlando attractions like Disney World and Universal Studios 🌊 Swimming, water sports, and student life events 🎭 Student-run clubs like Film Club, Gaming Club, Performing Arts, and Sports & Recreation Explore Further Want to learn more about the Summer for Success? Here you can explore a few short videos about the program, including insights from past students, parents, and staff. Hear from a Summer for Success Student What’s it like to be a Summer for Success student? In this brief video, hear from Ella (SFS’23) on what the courses, faculty and environment are like at Beacon! Building Social Skills and Independence Hear from Abbey, Summer for Success instructor, on her favorite thing about the program: how students build confidence and independence in preparation for college life. Download the Brochure For more information or to share this program with your family or students, you can access, print, or download a digital flipbook version of our current brochure. Read Now Scholarships Scholarships are available for accepted students with demonstrated need and are awarded on a first-come, first-served basis. To apply, complete and return the scholarship application form below. Download How to Apply Student Eligibility To be eligible for the Summer for Success, you must be a current high school freshman, sophomore, junior or senior in the 2025–26 academic year and have a diagnosed learning disability such as dyslexia, ADHD, or a related condition. Complete Your Online Application To apply, please create a Beacon College online application account via the link below. Once you have completed the sign up form, you will receive an email to activate your account and create your password. You can then “Start a New Application,” and enter your anticipated high school graduation year to view the Beacon College programs you are eligible for and select the Summer for Success. Begin Application Submit Required Documents In order to process your application, we will require: Your high school transcript(s) Two completed summer program reference forms or letters of recommendation from a teacher, counselor, or professional who knows you well (non-family) Proof of a learning disability (IEP, 504 plan, psychoeducational evaluation, or related documentation) These can be uploaded through our online application system, emailed directly to admissions@beaconcollege.edu or emailed to your admissions counselor. Complete a Family Interview A family interview is also required to consider your application for admission. Upon receipt of your application documents, our Center for College Readiness staff will contact you to schedule your family interview. More Information The Summer for Success is our most popular program and fills up quickly each year. We encourage you to explore your summer options early and connect with our team if you have questions! We also offer live virtual information sessions regularly throughout the academic year where you can learn more and ask questions. Click the link below to sign up for an upcoming information session or to watch the most recent session recording. Information Session Learn More About Summer for Success Do you have a question? Get in touch with the Center for College Readiness at collegereadiness@beaconcollege.edu , or call 855-220-5376 (toll-free). Apply Today Request Info Plan a Visit RESOURCES Directory Campus Map Alumni Email Portal MyBeacon Portal Canvas Tech Support For Media WORKING AT BEACON Career Opportunities Faculty/Staff Portal Student Employment Giving Beacon College’s EASE Grant Performance Measures If you’re having accessibility issues, please let us know . Contact Us (855) 220-5374 Address 105 East Main Street Leesburg, Florida 34748 Follow Us © 2026 Beacon College. Web Design by PHOS Creative Sitemap Privacy Policy Accessibility Title VI Title IX Hi there! I’m here to help you find what you're looking for."
    },
